{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"There is one more genuine bandwidth-side optimization worth testing: store each `(cos, sin)` BF16 pair as one packed 32-bit word and return two strided views of that shared buffer. This preserves the required shapes and values while halving the number of store instructions; I’ll validate it against the reference locally before using a verification attempt."}}
